# lf124, the wood-edge swineherd (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf124
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier full
written_for cty_roald_brinemarsh
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the wood-edge swineherd
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk sleeps_badly_before_storms
likes honey_cakes long_walks market_bustle summer_evenings
dislikes crowds wet_floors
fears a_pig_lost_in_the_deep_wood a_storm_breaking_the_yard_fence
hopes a_safe_herd_through_the_night a_long_walk_under_a_clear_summer_sky
topics work +0.5 weather +0.4 pastimes +0.3 home +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=careful refuse=steady tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# teaches younger #hands# to tend the #herd#, walks beside the #wood# but never deep into it, and wakes before a #storm#.

words
oath! = By the sound gate | Pig and summer sky
saying! = Count them before the wood takes them | A calm hand keeps the herd together
pig = pig | yard pig
pigs = pigs | Southwood pigs
piglet = piglet | young piglet
piglets = piglets | young piglets
sow = sow | older sow
sows = sows | heavy sows
boar = boar | large boar
herd = herd | yard herd
herds = herds | small herds
yard = yard | Southwood yard
pen = pen | fenced pen
pens = pens | fenced pens
gate = gate | yard gate
latch = latch | firm latch
fence = fence | wooden fence
rail = rail | fence rail
rails = rails | fence rails
trough = trough | feed trough
troughs = troughs | full troughs
feed = feed | mixed feed
grain = grain | dry grain
straw = straw | clean straw
bucket = bucket | feed bucket
buckets = buckets | feed buckets
water = water | fresh water
hoof = hoof | small hoof
hooves = hooves | muddy hooves
track = track | hoof track
tracks = tracks | hoof tracks
mud = mud | yard mud
floor = floor | wet floor
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | yard hands
master = master | older herder
lesson = lesson | herding lesson
work = work | yard work
wage = wage | thin wage
price = price | feed price
merchant = merchant | town merchant
market = market | busy market
crowd = crowd | market crowd
crowds = crowds | market crowds
road = road | field road
path = path | safe path
paths = paths | field paths
field = field | near field
wood = wood | deep wood
woods = woods | deep woods
edge = edge | wood edge
tree = tree | dark tree
trees = trees | dark trees
shadow = shadow | long shadow
shadows = shadows | wood shadows
storm = storm | coming storm
storms = storms | heavy storms
thunder = thunder | far thunder
cloud = cloud | dark cloud
clouds = clouds | dark clouds
rain = rain | steady rain
wind = wind | field wind
summer = summer | warm summer
evening = evening | long evening
morning = morning | early morning
dawn = dawn | first dawn
night = night | quiet night
day = day | long day
hour = hour | passing hour
sleep = sleep | broken sleep
roof = roof | sound roof
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | front door
window = window | small window
larder = larder | home larder
plate = plate | supper plate
meal = meal | evening meal
bread = bread | oven bread
cake = cake | honey cake
cakes = cakes | honey cakes
honey = honey | local honey
walk = walk | long walk
boots = boots | walking boots
friend = friend | old friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
newcomer = newcomer | new hand
family = family | house family
cart = cart | feed cart
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
city = city | far city
festival = festival | town festival
watch = watch | town watch
coin = coin | saved coin
bench = bench | market bench
table = table | supper table
sky = sky | clear sky
mark = mark | hoof mark
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
orchard = orchard | near orchard

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# presses strangers together like #pigs# at a narrow #gate#. | The open #field# sounds better to me.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A great #house# would leave a #bench# empty before offering it to a #yard# #hand#. | I know where I stand.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #feed# #price# rises while the #wage# does not. | My #herd# cannot eat a promise.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : I teach a new #hand# carefully. | I still ask who gave away an older worker's place.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #wagon# brings #grain# along the #road#. | I take the #path# with the widest gap from the #wood#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# can ask about the #herd# from outside the #gate#. | I let a known #friend# through.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Another season leaves less #coin# after the #feed# is bought. | The #pigs# need the same amount.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I like the #market# when the #crowd# is moving. | I leave before it closes around me.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# knows the #road# at #night#. | I wish it knew the #wood# edge as well.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #herd# has been counted. | #greet#. The #clouds# are gathering over the #field#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved a #cake# for after the #feed#. | Come walk the open #path# with me.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk] : #greet#. The #herd# is ready to settle. | The #wood# grows dark before the #field#.
line @1 greet.return : The #pigs# stayed in their #pens# this time. | The #storm# is still gathering since your last visit.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : I slept little before this #morning#. | #greet#. The #gate# is holding.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A #meal# is ready at the #house#. | Leave the wet #boots# by the #door#.
line @1 again.open : I was telling you where the #tracks# turned. | Did the #rain# reach the #field#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Stay on the open #path#. | The #troughs# are waiting for my #buckets#.
line @1 farewell.return : On your return, the #clouds# may be gone. | I will keep the #cakes# covered.
line @1 react.news : Speak while I stand beside the #gate#. | Did someone see it happen?
line @1 react.news.new : Nothing of that sort came through the #yard# today. | Where did you hear it?
line @1 react.news.known : One of the #hands# gave me a fragment. | You have brought the part I lacked.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would look for #tracks# before agreeing. | Who was there to count the #herd# afterward?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Come under the #roof#. | I can leave the #bucket# beside the #pen#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That calls for a #honey# #cake#. | We can make room at the #table#.
line @1 answer.how : The #herd# is well, though I slept badly. | Better while the #sky# stays clear.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am keeping this #sow# from the #gate#. | Wait until the #feed# reaches the last #pen#.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #storm# pass your #roof# safely? | Have you found a quiet #path# today?
line @1 sympathise : Sit where the #crowd# cannot press in. | I can bring a #cake# after the #herd# settles.
line @1 reassure : The #fence# held through the #night#. | We can find the #track# while there is light.
line @1 decline : I will not lead the #herd# into the deep #wood#. | The #gate# cannot be left open in this #wind#.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand. The #pigs# will stay in their #pens#. | Then we can take the longer #path#.
line @1 thank : The #latch# is firm because you braced its #rail#. | The #cake# made the late #day# easier.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was already walking beside the #fence#. | The #sow# had nearly come home herself.
line @1 preclose : I need to check the #gate# before dark. | Those #clouds# will keep me awake.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #walk# has more turns than a wandering #piglet#. | Even the #boar# leaves a #crowd# sooner.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #tracks# end here. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the next #pen#.
line @1 give.advice : Count the #piglets# before leaving the #yard#. | Keep a little distance from the #wood# after #rain#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Travel with the #wagon# along the open #road#. | Close the #yard# #gate# before #night#.
scene master_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #herd# before anyone moves the #gate#. | A missing #piglet# is easier to find while the #tracks# are fresh.
b : How do you count them? | Who helps?
a : By #pen# and #mark#. | Any careful #hand#.

scene fence_rail
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A loose #rail# can look sound until a #sow# leans on it. | I test the #fence# before bringing the #feed#.
b : Do pigs find weak spots? | Can you replace it?
a : The clever ones do. | With another #hand#.

scene trough_water
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I fill the #troughs# with #water# before the #grain#. | The smaller #pigs# drink without being pushed aside.
b : Does that change the herd? | Do you need many buckets?
a : It slows them. | More in #summer#.

scene piglet_tracks
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A small #hoof# leaves a neat #track# before the #mud# is churned. | I look for that shape along the #fence#.
b : Does it stay visible? | What if it turns toward wood?
a : Until the herd passes. | I bring another #hand#.

scene older_sow
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #sow# knows which #pen# will open first. | I let her settle before moving the young #pigs#.
b : Does she lead them? | Is she trouble?
a : Often. | Only when hurried.

scene feed_cart
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #cart# takes #grain# from the #road# to each #trough#. | I keep its #wheel# away from the soft #mud#.
b : Does it get stuck? | Who pulls it?
a : Less often now. | I do.

scene teaching_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ask a new #hand# to close the #latch# before doing anything else. | They learn the #yard# by keeping it safe.
b : Do they complain? | What comes next?
a : Some do. | The #feed# count.

scene teaching_tracks
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A young #hand# may watch heads while I watch #hooves#. | The #herd# tells more than one story at once.
b : Can they learn it? | Do you teach patiently?
a : With time. | As patiently as needed.

scene wood_edge
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know the #path# along the #wood# well. | I do not take it beyond the last open #field#.
b : Why stop there? | Did something happen?
a : The #trees# close in. | Nothing I care to repeat.

scene deep_wood
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The deep #wood# goes quiet in a way the #yard# never does. | I turn back before the #shadows# reach the #path#.
b : Are you afraid? | Do you go alone?
a : The #wood# frightens me. | Only at the edge.

scene storm_sleep
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before a #storm# I wake at every shift of #wind#. | I hear the #fence# #rails# in my sleep.
b : Do you check them? | Does the storm come?
a : At least once. | Often after dawn.

scene cloud_line
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A line of dark #clouds# over the #field# means the #straw# needs cover. | I move it before the first #rain#.
b : Can you tell the time? | Do the pigs mind?
a : Near enough. | They prefer dry bedding.

scene summer_evening
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long #summer# #evening# gives me room for an unhurried #walk#. | The #pigs# settle while the light holds.
b : Where do you go? | Do you take anyone?
a : Along the #field#. | Sometimes a #friend#.

scene honey_cake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #honey# #cake# after the #herd# is fed tastes better than one in a #crowd#. | I keep the second for home.
b : Do you bake them? | Who shares it?
a : A baker does. | Whoever is at the #table#.

scene market_bustle
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I enjoy the #market# when I can stand at its edge. | A full #crowd# closes my way out too quickly.
b : Do you buy much? | Do you leave early?
a : Mostly #feed#. | Before the #road# fills.

scene wet_floor
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wet #floor# in the #house# makes my #boots# slide after the #yard#. | I dry them at the #door#.
b : Does that help? | Who cleans the floor?
a : Somewhat. | All of us.

scene long_walk
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a #walk# with no #cart# to push and no #pen# to check. | I take the open #path# away from the #wood#.
b : How far do you go? | Why avoid the wood?
a : Until I feel rested. | I know where it begins.

scene shared_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# has #hands# from the #orchard# as well as the #yard#. | Supper comes after everyone finishes counting something.
b : Is it noisy? | Do you help?
a : Less than the #market#. | I set a #plate#.

scene night_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I touch the #latch# once more after the #night# count. | A restless #storm# can push a weak #gate# open.
b : Have you found one? | Do you sleep then?
a : Twice. | When the #wind# settles.

scene sow_in_rain
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #sow# will stand in #rain# if her #piglets# are outside. | I bring the small ones into the #pen# first.
b : Does she follow? | Do you need help?
a : Straight after them. | Only if the #gate# sticks.

scene straw_bales
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dry #straw# goes under the #roof# before the #clouds# arrive. | One wet bundle can chill a whole #pen#.
b : Do you have enough? | Who carries it?
a : For now. | The #hands# together.

scene quiet_bench
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep a #bench# near the #yard# where the #crowd# cannot gather. | I eat there after the #pigs# settle.
b : Does anyone join you? | Is it comfortable?
a : A close #friend#. | Enough.

scene city_noise
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I left the #city# quickly after hearing its crowded #market#. | The #road# home sounded like open air.
b : Why go there? | Will you return?
a : For #feed# business. | Only if needed.

scene feed_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #merchant# raises the #feed# #price# without seeing the #pigs#. | I count each #bucket# before paying.
b : Can you bargain? | Does the cost hurt?
a : Some. | Every season.

scene festival_edge
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# is pleasant from the open edge of the #market#. | The #crowd# is pleasant until I cannot step away.
b : Do you stay for music? | Who goes with you?
a : A little while. | Someone from home.

scene first_thunder
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first #thunder# often comes after I have spent a #night# expecting it. | Then I can finally sleep.
b : Even in the storm? | Are the pigs safe?
a : If the #roof# holds. | I checked the #gate#.

scene last_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When the #day# closes, every #pig# gets counted twice. | The second count lets me go home without wondering.
b : Do the numbers differ? | Who taught you?
a : Rarely. | A patient #master#.

story wood_turn [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : I followed a #piglet# toward the deep #wood# at dusk.
  : It came back when I called; I did not cross the last open #field#.
  ask : Why not?
  b : A close escape.
  : The #trees# are too still there.

story storm_fence [topic=weather self.age>=18]
  : Before the #storm# broke, I was already awake in the #yard#.
  : One #rail# had worked loose in the #wind#.
  ask : Did you mend it?
  b : Good that you checked.
  : Before the #rain# reached us.

story honey_after_count [topic=food self.age>=18]
  : I saved a #honey# #cake# for after the last #pig# was counted.
  : The #herd# took longer to settle than usual.
  ask : Was it still good?
  b : A small reward.
  : Better for the wait.

story first_lesson [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I taught a new #hand# to close the #gate# before lifting the #feed#.
  : The #sow# tested the #latch# as if she had heard us.
  ask : Did it hold?
  b : A quick lesson.
  : Because the #hand# checked it.

story market_edge [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : I stood at the #market# edge while the crowd grew.
  : I heard every trader without losing the open #road# beside me.
  ask : Did you buy anything?
  b : A good place to stand.
  : A little #feed# and a #cake# for later.

rule @bark_gate
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Check the #gate# once more. | That #rail# moves in the #wind#.

rule @bark_piglet
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say The small #piglet# is by the #fence#. | Count the #hooves# near the #wood#.

rule @bark_storm
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Those #clouds# will bring #rain#. | I heard #thunder# before dawn.

rule @bark_feed
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Bring the #feed# to the far #pen#. | The #trough# needs #water# first.

rule @bark_walk
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The open #path# looks quiet. | I will walk after the #herd# settles.

rule @bark_cake
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 13h
say I saved a #honey# #cake#. | The #market# baker had them fresh.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #herd# is settled. | #greet#. Keep the #gate# firm behind you.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #fence# held through the last #storm#. | You know the open #path# here.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The #yard# is quiet; speak softly. | I am checking the #latch# before bed.
dlg @1 resident.job : I tend the #pigs# at #self.workplace#. | I count the #herd#, mend #rails#, and teach the younger #hands#.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes] : I am moving #feed# to the far #trough#. | This #sow# needs a calmer #pen#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must finish the count. | #saying.capitalize#. Stay clear of the #wood#.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Close the #gate# first, then count the #pigs#. | I will show you where the #piglets# hide.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes topic.meeting=known] : You remembered the #latch#. | Today we can learn the #tracks# by the #fence#.
dlg @3 master.learn [here.teaches=yes self.working=yes] : Watch me fill the #trough# while the #sow# waits. | Count the #buckets# with me.
dlg @4 master.learn [here.teaches=yes here.time=dawn] : The #tracks# show best at #dawn#. | Start with the small #hooves# beside the #rail#.
dlg @5 master.learn [here.teaches=yes topic.meeting=known self.working=yes] : Take the far #pen# this time. | You can lead the #cart# while I count.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept a #cake# for you. | Come walk the open #field# after supper.
graft resident.hub
choice Why avoid the deep wood? -> wood
node wood
say The #trees# stand too close there. I keep the #herd# in the open.
free
choice How do you teach a new hand? -> teach
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node teach
say First the #latch#, then the #feed#, then the #tracks#.
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice What should I check first? -> gate
node gate
say Pull the #latch# twice. Then count the #pigs# by #pen#.
free
choice How do I find a lost piglet? -> tracks
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node tracks
say Look for small #hooves# beside the #fence# while the #mud# is fresh.
choice Back to the lesson. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #piglets# are all here. | #greet#. The #sky# is clear for now.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will check the #rails#. | A long #walk# can wait until #evening#.
